# .trivyignore — suppress known false positives or accepted risks.
#
# Format: one AVD/CVE ID per line with a comment explaining why it is accepted.
# Keep this list as short as possible — prefer fixing over ignoring.

# ── S3 frontend bucket — intentionally public for static website hosting ──────
# All findings below relate to the frontend S3 bucket which serves a public
# static website. Public access is required by design. No sensitive data is
# stored here — only HTML, CSS, and JS assets.

AVD-AWS-0094    # S3 public access block disabled — frontend website bucket (by design)
AVD-AWS-0132    # S3 not encrypted — public static assets, no sensitive data

AWS-0086        # S3 block public ACL — frontend website requires public ACL (by design)
AWS-0087        # S3 block public policy — frontend website requires public bucket policy
AWS-0091        # S3 ignore public ACL — frontend website bucket must allow public ACL
AWS-0092        # S3 not publicly accessible via ACL — frontend website requires public-read ACL
AWS-0093        # S3 restrict public bucket — frontend website requires public access

AWS-0089        # S3 bucket logging not enabled — static assets only, no sensitive data
AWS-0090        # S3 versioning not enabled — static single-version deployment, no versioning needed

# ── RDS deletion protection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dev and staging have deletion_protection = false for easy teardown.
# Production has deletion_protection = true in terraform/environments/prod/main.tf.
# AVD-AWS-0177  # uncomment to suppress RDS deletion-protection check across all envs
